※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4669
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4669 LANG_ITERATOR_NOT_AN_ARRAY

※ A generator gives its values one at a time; nothing says how many there
※ will be, so there is no array to build out of its call.

fn count(n: u8) ⇉ u8:
    yield n

let std := ⎕import("std")

@[startup]
fn main(init: std.Init) → u6:
    let a: ⟦⟧ = count(1u8)
    0u6
